## Summary
At Optiver, a proprietary trading company, software engineering is evolving from prioritizing low-latency systems to emphasizing advanced AI models. The company maintains control over the full technology stack, including custom hardware, and operates with incentives distinct from typical tech firms.

## Key Points
- Shift in focus from latency to AI model development
- Full ownership of the technology stack from applications to custom hardware
- Unique incentive structures compared to other tech companies


